e else gets it i spoke to  falcons coach dan quinn  uh last saturday and i asked him because  that was the same day that cam newton's  positive test came to life there was  changes to the patriots chiefs game  i asked quinn what did you learn from  the situation with aj terrell who the  previous saturday  had had a positive test the he was  isolated as you do under the protocols  no other falcons players had tested  positive and they played their game  without issue and quinn said it was two  things one  aj was really diligent with wearing his  mask and two  he had no violations on the traffic  report because every  team every day your trainer whoever it  is is communicating with the company  that reads  the tracking devices the connection  tracking devices and the data that those  put out  of were you within some six feet of  somebody for 15 consecutive minutes  if you were then you that is flagged ave  tarot didn't have anything i mean it's  it's an oversimplification on some level  but it really can be this simple at a  very base level which is  wear a mask and keep your distance and  you're not going to infect other people  even if you yourself end up getting  infected tom pelicero my colleague from  the nfl network nfl media group joining  me here  uh on the rich eisen show to discuss um  i uh let's move on right now  uh to the tennessee titans where do  things stand on on the titans  um playing their next game and also  the investigation as to why  there it appears the titans  players decided to hold their own  practices after  being told to go home tom well that's  what the nfl and the nfl pa have been  looking into and they have  reviewed surveillance video they have  conducted interviews i can tell you that  with people in the organization as well  as with players trying to get to the  bottom of  you know how did those unauthorized  off-site workouts and i'm told there are  multiple involving multiple position  groups  how did those come together i know  th